# Client Hints merge (user-agent)

When editing Client Hints parsing or merge:

1. Read and apply `.agents/skills/client-hints/SKILL.md`.
2. Remember pipeline detectors run first; `merge.Apply` overlays CH last.

## Local norms

- Header parsing lives in `internal/hintparse` (RFC 8941 structured-field
  **subset** only—do not pull a full SF library).
- Public types and header extraction live in `useragent` (`ClientHints`,
  `ClientHintsFromHeader` / `FromMap`).
- Prefer Full-Version-List over Sec-CH-UA brands; use SignificantBrand for the
  meaningful brand (skip GREASE / “Not A;Brand”).
- On OS family conflict (e.g. Android UA + Windows CH), set
  `ClientHintsMismatch` and keep UA-derived OS fields.
- Frozen Chromium UA versions (`X.0.0.0`) should yield to richer CH versions.
- Preserve iPadOS when UA says iPadOS and CH says broader iOS.
- CLI hint flags must match wire values (often quoted); reproduce with
  `/parse-ua`.
